3040
01:54:32.190 --> 01:54:34.070
and if it's somebody, if, you know,

3041
01:54:34.070 --> 01:54:35.940
if somebody's written like a non-fiction book,

3042
01:54:35.940 --> 01:54:38.550
I'll kind of go through the structure of that book

3043
01:54:38.550 --> 01:54:40.710
and extract from that themes and principles

3044
01:54:40.710 --> 01:54:42.540
that I want to explore with the guest.

3045
01:54:42.540 --> 01:54:44.670
And I think the process of not just writing,

3046
01:54:44.670 --> 01:54:47.430
but then creating the outline, you know,

3047
01:54:47.430 --> 01:54:52.430
every little extra step cements the information

3048
01:54:52.770 --> 01:54:54.480
and the knowledge contained in the book

3049
01:54:54.480 --> 01:54:55.770
a little bit more deeply,

3050
01:54:55.770 --> 01:54:58.230
and then I'll review the outline and I'll refine the outline

3051
01:54:58.230 --> 01:54:59.700
and then I'll make extra notes.

3052
01:54:59.700 --> 01:55:02.400
So all of those little things, I think really help,

3053
01:55:02.400 --> 01:55:07.290
